{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792868134,"nonce":"dalaTmT0vzwTYvaQahUmxsvJmFE=","title":"TypeScript: abstract classes and abstract methods","message":"Abstract classes were Unsupported. An abstract class is declared like any class; an abstract method has a signature and no body, and a call through a base-typed receiver dispatches to the implementation of the instance's class, since no instance of the abstract class itself exists. Checked as TypeScript does: instantiating an abstract class (2511), a concrete subclass missing an inherited abstract method (2515), super.m() on an abstract method (2513), and abstract methods without a return type (7010). Unsupported: abstract properties, abstract members outside abstract classes or on statics and accessors, and calls of an abstract method no class implements.","files":null}]}